{\rtf\ansi \deff0{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue128;}{\fonttbl{\f0
\fcharset0\fnil Arial;}}\plain\cf1\fs20 \pard Finally, we compare the 
reproduction to the original signal.  Note that the Amplification 
Factor (A)\par was chosen for minimum error under noiseless 
conditions.  A table comparing the various errors for\par specific 
noise factors (variance) shows that the system is relatively noise 
intolerant.  By noise \par intolerant, we mean a reproduction with an 
absolute error below 10.  There is a good reason for\par this: a noise 
factor above .001 produces a signal that, graphically, obviously 
devites from the \par original.  The application dictates whether the 
reproduction is satisfactory. }
